===
# Compare: Old vs New Syntax

**Old way** (explicit grid):
```
::: {display: 'grid'; grid-template-columns: '1fr 1fr'; gap: '2em'}
:::
```

**New way** (shorthand):
```
::: {columns: 2; gap: 30}
:::
```

Both produce identical output!

===
# Old Syntax Still Works

This uses the old explicit syntax:
::: {display: 'grid'; grid-template-columns: '1fr 1fr'; gap: '2em'}
### Traditional Left
Using explicit CSS grid properties

### Traditional Right
Backward compatibility maintained
:::

